From: Alex Gonzalez <alexg@balena.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Aug 2024 16:10:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mach-imx: hab: allow to specify custom IVT offset from
 environment

This allows to boot a signed Linux kernel with an initramfs bundle, and
not only a signed Image file where the offset is automatically detected
from the headers.

Include env.h, which U-Boot no longer includes implicitly since it removed
common.h.

Signed-off-by: Alex Gonzalez <alexg@balena.io>

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm/mach-imx/hab.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/hab.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/hab.c
index ab586157..fe2d9f2d 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/hab.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/hab.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <command.h>
 #include <config.h>
 #include <display_options.h>
+#include <env.h>
 #include <fuse.h>
 #include <mapmem.h>
 #include <image.h>
@@ -1026,7 +1027,9 @@ int authenticate_image(u32 ddr_start, u32 raw_image_size)
 	u32 ivt_offset;
 	size_t bytes;
 
-	ivt_offset = (raw_image_size + ALIGN_SIZE - 1) &
+	ivt_offset = env_get_hex("ivt_offset", 0);
+	if ( !ivt_offset )
+		ivt_offset = (raw_image_size + ALIGN_SIZE - 1) &
 					~(ALIGN_SIZE - 1);
 	bytes = ivt_offset + IVT_SIZE + CSF_PAD_SIZE;
 
